      section_group(
        label: "1a · Host state frontier — machines are stateful; declare the boundary (operator, 2026-07-22)",
        nodes: [
          ticket_row(id: "ts-host-state", done: false, t: TicketFields {
            headline: "the gap, named: workflows over host state we neither guarantee nor model",
            brief: "Our deploy/subsumption workflows are causal scripts over host state we neither guarantee nor model — and host state is effectively infinitely permutable, so any workflow whose correctness depends on unmodeled state is untenable. The doctrine half-exists (observe→diff→converge, gunbc.ownership, fail-closed observation); the gap is that THE BOUNDARY OF THE MODELED STATE IS UNDECLARED. Resolution is NOT model-everything — observe-all is the absorbing trap in reverse — it is shrink-the-state-that-matters: content-addressed desired state + idempotent converge + readback. The children are the three mechanisms.",
            displaced_cost: "both 2026-07-22 tail incidents happened exactly at the undeclared boundary: reading foreign state without a contract (the runner checkout's live .git); blanket-copying foreign state into owned state (the leaked extraheader)",
            current_state: "the gap fired live (srv4, 2026-07-23): srv4 OOM-killed PR CI. Two layers — srv4 was NOT a modeled fleet member (no fleet_intent row; #7027 carries the enrollment), and the converge model has NO live actuator (KnobUnimplemented at PerSlotMemoryCap; the bash-emit path unprovable with zero executing consumers — every fabric model is paper, now priced). Interim hand-fix applied with derived-equal values; every row owed a modeled axis with dissolution",
            first_slice: "the 0-to-3 dispatch brief (2026-07-23): kill the bash-emit transport (runtime-present hosts converge through typed effects only); close the loop vertically on PerSlotMemoryCap (idempotence + perturb-and-heal + foreign-occupant receipts on srv1); enroll srv4 + the enrollment wall (a host takes no fleet work without an intent row); the axis-bundle framework with interference DERIVED from provider fact rows — claims as verb-by-subtree facts, conflict = computed claim intersection, never a named domain or hand candidate roster (operator ruling 2026-07-23)",
            red_control: "unmodeled occupants of a claimed resource position refuse as typed findings; TakeoverRuling is the only signed path from foreign occupant to owned teardown",
            out_of_scope: "",
            handback: "",
            updates: [
              TicketUpdate { on: "2026-07-25", note: "migrated to ticket form (W2-bulk tranche 6); the srv4 receipts and the 0-to-3 brief preserved in their fields with their dates" },
            ],
            authored_on: "",
            last_verified_on: "",
          }),
          ticket_row(id: "ts-host-frontier", done: false, t: TicketFields {
            headline: "declared state frontier per host-touching workflow",
            brief: "Every state input/output classified Derived (regenerable from spec; delete-and-recreate always legal) | OwnedMember (observed + reconciled by identity — the membership spine) | ForeignWithContract (someone else's process, read only through a NAMED contract); unclassified refuses. This is the group-of-units taxonomy applied to host state; extends gunbc.ownership.",
            displaced_cost: "implicit reads of foreign state — the tree-sync whitelist (#7086) became a four-item declared contract by INCIDENT, not at authoring time",
