            headline: "structural exit — the derivable red class heals itself on PRs; main drift fails CI",
            brief: "A generated-artifact drift is a red whose remedy is a pure function of the tree: regenerate the projection from its .dag authority. The heal job (pull_request only) checks out the PR source branch head, runs main_wet, and commits+pushes the fix back to that branch only when git diff shows a change — a drifted PR is repaired on its own branch before it reaches main. main is deliberately NOT auto-healed: its ci drift gate reds honestly, which is the correct main behavior.",
            displaced_cost: "hand-fixing derivable drift reds per PR",
